# Response-shape gate ratchet. MAY ONLY SHRINK.
# An entry here is a tool DTO property with no matching property on the server type its route
# produces. Two kinds live here:
#   (a) a genuine mismatch not yet fixed — fix it and delete the line;
#   (b) a server shape the analyser cannot see statically (private record, anonymous
#       Results.Ok(new { ... })) — the comment must say so.
# NEVER add a line to make a build pass. Fix the DTO instead.
#
# Key format:
#   <ToolClass>.<Dto>.<Property>   a property the paired server type does not send   (kind a)
#   <ToolClass>.<Dto>              the server shape could not be resolved at all     (kind b)
#
# A kind (b) entry means that DTO is UNCHECKED, not that it is correct. It is listed rather than
# skipped precisely so the unchecked surface stays visible and countable. The way to remove one is
# to give the endpoint a named response type (.Produces<T>() or a typed result) — then the gate
# checks it and the line goes.

# ── (a) GENUINE MISMATCHES — the endpoint is typed, the tool asks for something it never sends ──
# These are live defects in the served MCP surface, not analyser limitations. Left for the tool-
# fixing tasks; every one of them silently deserializes to null/0 today.
ActionSubmitTool.SubmitResponse.Message           # ActionSubmissionResponse has no 'message' at all
ActionSubmitTool.NextActionDto.Title              # NextActionResponse sends 'actionTitle', not 'title'
ActionSubmitTool.NextActionDto.AssignedTo         # NextActionResponse sends 'participantId', not 'assignedTo'
BlueprintUpdateTool.BlueprintResponse.Status      # Blueprint has no 'status' property
BlueprintUpdateTool.BlueprintResponse.ModifiedAt  # Blueprint sends 'updatedAt', not 'modifiedAt'

# ── (b) SERVER SHAPE NOT STATICALLY REACHABLE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same limitation Sorcha.Cli.ContractTests documents in its NotAWireContract list: a handler
# declared Task<IResult> returning Results.Ok(new { ... }) names no type, so there is nothing for
# the tool DTO to be compared against.

